This license covers everything in the "enterprise/" directory of this
repository (the "Enterprise Software"), plus the "worker/" directory and the
release and deploy scripts at the repository root. It does not cover "core/",
which is a separate project (VoltrusID/voltrus-scada) licensed under the GNU
Affero General Public License v3.0 or later. It does not cover "sdks/", which is
MIT licensed where a LICENSE file in that directory says so.

The source code of the Enterprise Software is visible so that you can read it,
audit it and learn from it. It is source available, not open source. Reading the
code does not give you the right to run it in production.

1. What you may do without a subscription

   You may:
   a. Read, clone and study the Enterprise Software.
   b. Build and run it on your own machines for evaluation, development and
      testing, including automated tests, for as long as you need. Do not use it
      for production work or to run a live process, site or business.
   c. Modify it for those same evaluation, development and testing purposes.
   d. Submit contributions to this repository under the terms in section 6.

2. What needs a paid subscription

   Production use of the Enterprise Software requires a valid, paid Voltrus
   Enterprise subscription or licence, shown by a licence key issued by
   JoyoDigitama. Production use means running the Enterprise Software, or any
   build made from it, to monitor, control or report on a real site, plant,
   customer or business, or offering it to others as a hosted or managed
   service. Each licence key covers the sites and terms stated in your order.
   Current plans and prices: https://voltrus.id/voltrus-scada

3. Licence keys and the licence check

   The Enterprise Software contains a licence check. You must not:
   a. Remove, bypass, disable or weaken the licence check, or make a build
      behave as if a valid licence key is present when it is not.
   b. Forge, generate, copy, share, resell or publish licence keys or
      activation files, or the keys used to sign them.
   c. Change the trusted signing keys, the grace period, the tier limits or the
      feature flags in a way that unlocks features you have not paid for.
   d. Use a licence key on more sites or devices than your order allows.

   Fixing a genuine defect in the licence check is welcome. Report it to
   support@voltrus.id first and do not use it to get features for free.

4. Distribution

   You may not sell, sublicense, rent or distribute the Enterprise Software, in
